
*** Running Tests ***

A correctness test using GoogleTest is provided in the `test` directory.
To run the tests, first build the project with testing enabled (which is the default in the updated CMake configuration).

  $ cd build
  $ cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DMPI_CXX='...' ...
  $ cmake --build .

Then you can run the test executable directly:

  $ ./test/lulesh_test.exe

Or use CTest:

  $ ctest -C Release


More information including LULESH 1.0 can be found at https://codesign.llnl.gov/lulesh.php

If you have any questions or problems please contact:

Ian Karlin <karlin1@llnl.gov> or
Rob Neely <neely4@llnl.gov>

Also please send any notable results to Ian Karlin <karlin1@llnl.gov> as we are still evaluating the performance of this code.

A Makefile and a CMake build system are provided.

*** Building with CMake ***

Create a build directory and run cmake. Example:

  $ mkdir build; cd build; cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DMPI_CXX_COMPILER=`which mpicxx` ..
  $ cmake --build .

When building on Windows, you can use the following commands:

  $ cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DMPI_CXX='g++ -DUSE_MPI=1 -I$(MPI_INC) -L$(MPI_LIB) -lmsmpi' --log-level=VERBOSE ..
  $ cmake --build .

Where MPI_INC points to the Microsoft MPI include directory and MPI_LIB points to the Microsoft MPI lib directory. On my personal machine, these are...

MPI_INC = D:\Microsoft SDKs\MPI\Include
MPI_LIB = D:\Microsoft SDKs\MPI\Lib\x64

On Windows I installed mingw64 for my compilers, cmake tooling, etc. and added it to my path ("D:\mingw64\bin"). You will need to adjust the paths to match your installation.

CMake variables:

  CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE      "Debug", "Release", or "RelWithDebInfo"

  CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER    Path to the C++ compiler
  MPI_CXX_COMPILER      Path to the MPI C++ compiler

  WITH_MPI=On|Off       Build with MPI (Default: On)
  WITH_OPENMP=On|Off    Build with OpenMP support (Default: On)
  WITH_SILO=On|Off      Build with support for SILO. (Default: Off).
  
  SILO_DIR              Path to SILO library (only needed when WITH_SILO is "On")

*** Building and Running a Plain, Serial Version of LULESH ***

As a sanity check, you can test whether the code is working without MPI or OpenMP by using the following commands to build it:

  $ cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DWITH_MPI=Off -DWITH_OPENMP=Off --log-level=VERBOSE ..
  $ cmake --build .

Call the resulting binary with:

  $ ./lulesh2.0 -p

to run with default values for the parameters, with -p allowing you to see the progress of the simulation. If it works, you should see
something like this...

```
$ .\lulesh2.0 -p
